    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-36005",
      "knowledge_point_id": "e3991a54-342b-5cd0-87e2-606146240555",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Gradient of a Function of Two Variables",
      "problem": "Evaluate $∇h(x,y)$ at $(1,1)$ if $h(x,y)=4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the partial derivatives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y \\\\ {h}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y) \\\\  & =\\frac{4x}{{y}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇h(x,y) & =⟨{h}_{x}(x,y),\\,{h}_{y}(x,y)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y,\\,\\frac{4x}{{y}^{2}+1}⟩ \\\\ ∇h(1,1) & =⟨4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1,\\,\\frac{4\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}+1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{4}{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\pi ,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "⟨\\pi ,\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩"
